This README file contains information on the contents of the
meta-user layer.

Please see the corresponding sections below for details.


Overview
========

meta-user is the UEI board support layer for the PetaLinux 2026.1
(Yocto Scarthgap) UEI Zynq UltraScale+ products. It lives in
project-spec/meta-user of the PetaLinux project and provides:

  - Machine settings (conf/machine/include/uei-zynq-base.inc) shared by the
    zu3eg, zu4eg, zu4ev, zu4ev-tsn, zu4eg-tsn and zu9eg-tsn machines.
  - Linux kernel: linux-xlnx 6.18.40 (PREEMPT_RT) with UEI patches and
    configuration (recipes-kernel/linux), plus the UEI out-of-tree modules
    kernel-module-daqiomc and kernel-module-ueitsn.
  - Bootloader and device-tree customizations (recipes-bsp/u-boot,
    recipes-bsp/device-tree).
  - Images (recipes-core/images):
      uei-image-sec-zynq       main hardened image (SELinux, TPM2, OpenSCAP)
      uei-image-sdk-zynq       SDK/development image
      uei-image-recovery-zynq  minimal SWUpdate recovery image
    and the WIC layout with main and recovery rootfs (wic/rootfs.wks).

Conf files:

  conf/layer.conf          layer registration (priority 7, scarthgap)
  conf/petalinuxbsp.conf   PetaLinux BSP settings, including the source
                           mirror (SOURCE_MIRROR_URL) used for offline builds
  conf/user-rootfsconfig   user rootfs package entries for petalinux-config -c rootfs

In the offline-bsp branch the UEI packages are fetched as checksummed
tarballs from the source mirror instead of SVN. Recipes disabled for the
offline build are kept with a "-nouse" suffix. See the top-level README.md
for build steps.


Dependencies
============

This layer depends on the layers provided by the PetaLinux 2026.1 project:

  URI: git://git.openembedded.org/bitbake
  branch: 2.8 (scarthgap)

  URI: git://git.openembedded.org/openembedded-core
  layers: meta
  branch: scarthgap

  PetaLinux/Xilinx layers (meta-xilinx-core, meta-xilinx-tools, meta-petalinux)
  and the other layers used by the recipes in this layer, e.g.
  meta-openembedded, meta-swupdate, meta-qt5, meta-selinux, meta-security,
  meta-tpm and meta-virtualization.


Patches
=======

Please submit any patches against the meta-user layer to the UEI
engineering team and cc: the maintainer:

Maintainer: UEI Engineering


Table of Contents
=================

  I. Adding the meta-user layer to your build
 II. Misc


I. Adding the meta-user layer to your build
=================================================

In a PetaLinux project the layer is added automatically once this
repository is placed in project-spec/meta-user (see the top-level
README.md).

For a plain Yocto build, add the location of the meta-user layer to
bblayers.conf, along with any other layers needed. e.g.:

  BBLAYERS ?= " \
    /path/to/yocto/meta \
    /path/to/yocto/meta-poky \
    /path/to/yocto/meta-yocto-bsp \
    /path/to/yocto/meta-user \
    "


II. Misc
========

Machine specific firmware (FSBL, PMUFW and bitstreams) and hardware
descriptions (XSA) are not part of this layer. They are in fw/ and hw/ at
the top of the repository, and scripts/build_qspi.sh uses them to create
the QSPI boot image.
